From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vipul Cariappa <vipulcariappa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:07:15 +0530
Subject: Reach a CppInterOp that is already in the process

The dispatch loader only ever resolved the API by dlopen'ing a path. An
embedding host that links or loads libclangCppInterOp itself owns the
interpreter, and a client that opens its own copy gets a second library with a
second, empty interpreter -- so nothing the host declared is visible to it. The
existing way out was for the client to name the very same file the host used,
which the client generally has no way to know, and which does not exist as a
path at all in a wasm build where the host may have linked the library rather
than loaded it.

Look for CppGetProcAddress in the process first, and only fall back to opening a
path when it is absent. dlopen(NULL) is the portable spelling of "the symbols
already here" and works under emscripten's dynamic linker as well as on ELF;
Windows gets the GetModuleHandle(NULL) equivalent.

A client that is genuinely alone in the process sees no change: the lookup
misses and the path is used exactly as before, so a bad path still fails and a
good one still succeeds.

(cherry picked from commit 0e8ef4b25dee9278d9cbb9bf570db2ec8404bbf3)
---
 include/CppInterOp/Dispatch.h | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/CppInterOp/Dispatch.h b/include/CppInterOp/Dispatch.h
index 9a7b5a0..095f045 100644
--- a/include/CppInterOp/Dispatch.h
+++ b/include/CppInterOp/Dispatch.h
@@ -61,6 +61,33 @@ inline void* dlGetProcAddress(const char* name,
   }
 
   std::call_once(*init, [customLibPath]() {
+    // A CppInterOp already in the process wins over any path. An embedding host
+    // that links or loads the library itself owns the interpreter, and a client
+    // that goes and opens its own copy gets a second library with a second,
+    // empty interpreter instead of the host's -- the symptom being that nothing
+    // the host declared is visible. Which file the host used, and whether it
+    // linked rather than dlopen'd, does not have to be known here: what matters
+    // is that the lookup goes through the copy that is already loaded.
+#ifdef _WIN32
+    if (HMODULE self = GetModuleHandleA(nullptr)) {
+      if (auto* proc = reinterpret_cast<void* (*)(const char*)>(
+              GetProcAddress(self, "CppGetProcAddress"))) {
+        getProc = proc;
+        return;
+      }
+    }
+#else
+    if (void* self = dlopen(nullptr, RTLD_LOCAL | RTLD_NOW)) {
+      // NOLINTNEXTLINE(cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast)
+      if (auto* proc = reinterpret_cast<void* (*)(const char*)>(
+              dlsym(self, "CppGetProcAddress"))) {
+        getProc = proc;
+        return;
+      }
+      dlclose(self);
+    }
+#endif
+
     const char* path =
         customLibPath ? customLibPath : std::getenv("CPPINTEROP_LIBRARY_PATH");
     if (!path)
